{
  "tema": 8578,
  "slug": "traer-llevar",
  "titulo": "Traer vs llevar",
  "subtitulo": "«Tráeme un café. Lleva esto a la oficina.»",
  "foto": "t05.jpg",
  "regla": "Traer = bring something toward where the speaker is (here). Llevar = take something away to another place (there). Spanish follows the speaker's position strictly, even where English says _bring_.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Traer** = movement **toward the speaker**: _bring (here)_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Llevar** = movement **away from the speaker**, to somewhere else: _take (there)_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Pronoun",
            "traer",
            "llevar"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "traigo",
              "llevo"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "traes",
              "llevas"
            ],
            [
              "él / ella / usted",
              "trae",
              "lleva"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "traemos",
              "llevamos"
            ],
            [
              "ellos / ustedes",
              "traen",
              "llevan"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The trap: English says _I'll **bring** wine to your party_. In Spanish you're not at the party yet, so it moves away from you: **Llevo vino a tu fiesta**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The host, who is at the party, says: **Trae vino**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It works like **venir** (come here) vs **ir** (go there): **traer** goes with **venir**, **llevar** with **ir**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Llevar** also means _to wear_ and _to carry_: **Llevo una sudadera**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "¿Me ==traes== un vaso de agua?",
              "en": "Can you bring me a glass of water?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Mañana ==llevo== la tabla a la playa.",
              "en": "Tomorrow I'm taking the board to the beach."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Trae== tu kimono a la clase.",
              "en": "Bring your gi to class. (said by the coach at the gym)"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Llevo== unas cervezas a la carne asada de Toño.",
              "en": "I'll bring some beers to Toño's barbecue."
            },
            {
              "es": "El mesero nos ==trae== la cuenta.",
              "en": "The waiter brings us the check."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Te ==llevo== al aeropuerto?",
              "en": "Shall I take you to the airport?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi mamá siempre ==trae== tamales cuando viene.",
              "en": "My mom always brings tamales when she comes over."
            },
            {
              "es": "Voy a ==llevar== estas plantas al huerto.",
              "en": "I'm going to take these plants to the garden."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
